    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "This is probably i find myself doing most and right now it seems treesitter only works with JS, and even then its spotty at best, for example some destructured argument `function({ a, b })` will break.\r\n\r\nAnd on top of that, it doesnt work in any other languages.\r\n\r\nDo any of your plugins do this? I searched around and `ai` seemed closest but it didnt seem to allow movement.\r\n\r\nSuch a great series of plugins youre doing, thank you !! 🎩",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">This is probably i find myself doing most and right now it seems treesitter only works with JS, and even then its spotty at best, for example some destructured argument <code class=\"notranslate\">function({ a, b })</code> will break.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">And on top of that, it doesnt work in any other languages.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Do any of your plugins do this? I searched around and <code class=\"notranslate\">ai</code> seemed closest but it didnt seem to allow movement.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Such a great series of plugins youre doing, thank you !! 🎩</p>",
    "bodyText": "This is probably i find myself doing most and right now it seems treesitter only works with JS, and even then its spotty at best, for example some destructured argument function({ a, b }) will break.\nAnd on top of that, it doesnt work in any other languages.\nDo any of your plugins do this? I searched around and ai seemed closest but it didnt seem to allow movement.\nSuch a great series of plugins youre doing, thank you !! 🎩",
