    "comment_count": 6,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "No module addresses this directly, no.\r\n\r\nWhat I use myself is a combination of next/prev [argument textobject](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/333d2d1090c80ac936b960469a6e93982cbaeb21/doc/mini-ai.txt#L163) from 'mini.ai' and [exchange operator](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/333d2d1090c80ac936b960469a6e93982cbaeb21/doc/mini-operators.txt#L231-L241) from 'mini.operators'. I have keymaps similar to this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.keymap.set('n', '<Leader>oh', '<Cmd>normal gxiagxila<CR>')\r\nvim.keymap.set('n', '<Leader>ol', '<Cmd>normal gxiagxina<CR>')\r\n```\r\n\r\nThey are **far from perfect**,  as `ina`/`ila` textobjects not always mean what I would like it to mean (in case of some complex nested arguments), but in non-nested cases it works good.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">No module addresses this directly, no.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">What I use myself is a combination of next/prev <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/333d2d1090c80ac936b960469a6e93982cbaeb21/doc/mini-ai.txt#L163\">argument textobject</a> from 'mini.ai' and <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/333d2d1090c80ac936b960469a6e93982cbaeb21/doc/mini-operators.txt#L231-L241\">exchange operator</a> from 'mini.operators'. I have keymaps similar to this:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"vim.keymap.set('n', '&lt;Leader&gt;oh', '&lt;Cmd&gt;normal gxiagxila&lt;CR&gt;')\nvim.keymap.set('n', '&lt;Leader&gt;ol', '&lt;Cmd&gt;normal gxiagxina&lt;CR&gt;')\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">keymap</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">set</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>n<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>&lt;Leader&gt;oh<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>&lt;Cmd&gt;normal gxiagxila&lt;CR&gt;<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>)\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">keymap</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">set</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>n<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>&lt;Leader&gt;ol<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>&lt;Cmd&gt;normal gxiagxina&lt;CR&gt;<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>)</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">They are <strong>far from perfect</strong>,  as <code class=\"notranslate\">ina</code>/<code class=\"notranslate\">ila</code> textobjects not always mean what I would like it to mean (in case of some complex nested arguments), but in non-nested cases it works good.</p>",
            "bodyText": "No module addresses this directly, no.\nWhat I use myself is a combination of next/prev argument textobject from 'mini.ai' and exchange operator from 'mini.operators'. I have keymaps similar to this:\nvim.keymap.set('n', '<Leader>oh', '<Cmd>normal gxiagxila<CR>')\nvim.keymap.set('n', '<Leader>ol', '<Cmd>normal gxiagxina<CR>')\nThey are far from perfect,  as ina/ila textobjects not always mean what I would like it to mean (in case of some complex nested arguments), but in non-nested cases it works good.",
