                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "No easy solution, I am afraid, as by default it `sort()` operator just compares strings with `<` and Lua does this case sensitively.\r\n\r\nYou can [override compare function](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/333d2d1090c80ac936b960469a6e93982cbaeb21/doc/mini-operators.txt#L461-L462), though.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">No easy solution, I am afraid, as by default it <code class=\"notranslate\">sort()</code> operator just compares strings with <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;</code> and Lua does this case sensitively.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">You can <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/333d2d1090c80ac936b960469a6e93982cbaeb21/doc/mini-operators.txt#L461-L462\">override compare function</a>, though.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "No easy solution, I am afraid, as by default it sort() operator just compares strings with < and Lua does this case sensitively.\nYou can override compare function, though.",
