        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1386207?u=2ea2ddf4c5356c8e8bffeace499e492f8e9becca&v=4",
                "login": "9mm",
                "resourcePath": "/9mm",
                "url": "https://github.com/9mm"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "NONE",
            "body": "Also one other easy `gs` question. Lets say I have this:\r\n\r\n```javascript\r\n    watch(accountId, () => {\r\n      fetchData();\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    return {\r\n      accountId,\r\n      accounts,\r\n      [c]olumns, <- cursor is here\r\n      data,\r\n      loading,\r\n      query,\r\n    };\r\n  },\r\n```\r\n\r\nHow do I sort everything in the `{`?\r\n\r\nI have tried `gsii, gsi{ gsip, gsai` and i cant seem to nail it right. I suspect `gsi{` should work, but it makes a weird result:\r\n\r\n```\r\n    return {\r\n      ,\r\n      accountId,\r\n      accounts,\r\n      columns,\r\n      data,\r\n      loading,query\r\n    };\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf i do the same selection of `vii` and then `:sort i` it does work however",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Also one other easy <code class=\"notranslate\">gs</code> question. Lets say I have this:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-js notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"    watch(accountId, () =&gt; {\n      fetchData();\n    });\n\n    return {\n      accountId,\n      accounts,\n      [c]olumns, &lt;- cursor is here\n      data,\n      loading,\n      query,\n    };\n  },\"><pre class=\"notranslate\">    <span class=\"pl-en\">watch</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s1\">accountId</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">=&gt;</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span>\n      <span class=\"pl-en\">fetchData</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>\n\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span>\n      accountId<span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span>\n      accounts<span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span>\n      <span class=\"pl-kos\">[</span><span class=\"pl-s1\">c</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">]</span>olumns<span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">-</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">cursor</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">is</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">here</span>\n      data<span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span>\n      loading<span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span>\n      query<span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">How do I sort everything in the <code class=\"notranslate\">{</code>?</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I have tried <code class=\"notranslate\">gsii, gsi{ gsip, gsai</code> and i cant seem to nail it right. I suspect <code class=\"notranslate\">gsi{</code> should work, but it makes a weird result:</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"    return {\n      ,\n      accountId,\n      accounts,\n      columns,\n      data,\n      loading,query\n    };\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">    return {\n      ,\n      accountId,\n      accounts,\n      columns,\n      data,\n      loading,query\n    };\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">If i do the same selection of <code class=\"notranslate\">vii</code> and then <code class=\"notranslate\">:sort i</code> it does work however</p>",
            "bodyText": "Also one other easy gs question. Lets say I have this:\n    watch(accountId, () => {\n      fetchData();\n    });\n\n    return {\n      accountId,\n      accounts,\n      [c]olumns, <- cursor is here\n      data,\n      loading,\n      query,\n    };\n  },\nHow do I sort everything in the {?\nI have tried gsii, gsi{ gsip, gsai and i cant seem to nail it right. I suspect gsi{ should work, but it makes a weird result:\n    return {\n      ,\n      accountId,\n      accounts,\n      columns,\n      data,\n      loading,query\n    };\n\nIf i do the same selection of vii and then :sort i it does work however",
