                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "> I have tried `gsii, gsi{ gsip, gsai` and i cant seem to nail it right. I suspect `gsi{` should work, but it makes a weird result:\r\n\r\nTry `gsVii` or `Viigs`. Default sort function [sorts charwise and linewise/blockwise regions differently](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/333d2d1090c80ac936b960469a6e93982cbaeb21/doc/mini-operators.txt#L435-L442).",
                    "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I have tried <code class=\"notranslate\">gsii, gsi{ gsip, gsai</code> and i cant seem to nail it right. I suspect <code class=\"notranslate\">gsi{</code> should work, but it makes a weird result:</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Try <code class=\"notranslate\">gsVii</code> or <code class=\"notranslate\">Viigs</code>. Default sort function <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/333d2d1090c80ac936b960469a6e93982cbaeb21/doc/mini-operators.txt#L435-L442\">sorts charwise and linewise/blockwise regions differently</a>.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "I have tried gsii, gsi{ gsip, gsai and i cant seem to nail it right. I suspect gsi{ should work, but it makes a weird result:\n\nTry gsVii or Viigs. Default sort function sorts charwise and linewise/blockwise regions differently.",
